{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Proximal Policy Optimization (PPO) Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: capture `log \u03c0_old(a | s)` at rollout time"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "for step in range(T):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    probs = softmax(logits(theta, state_features(s)))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    a = sample(probs, rng)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    s_next, r, done = env.step(s, a)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    buffer.append({"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"s\": s, \"a\": a, \"r\": r, \"done\": done,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"v_old\": value(w, state_features(s)),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"log_pi_old\": log(probs[a] + 1e-12),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    })"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    s = s_next"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The snapshot is taken once, at rollout time. It does not change during the update epochs."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: compute GAE advantages (Lesson 07)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Same as A2C. Normalize across the batch."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: clipped surrogate update"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "for _ in range(K_EPOCHS):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for mb in minibatches(buffer, size=64):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for rec in mb:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            x = state_features(rec[\"s\"])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            probs = softmax(logits(theta, x))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            logp = log(probs[rec[\"a\"]] + 1e-12)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            ratio = exp(logp - rec[\"log_pi_old\"])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            adv = rec[\"advantage\"]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            surrogate = min("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                ratio * adv,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                clamp(ratio, 1 - EPS, 1 + EPS) * adv,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            # backprop -surrogate, add value loss, subtract entropy"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            grad_logpi = onehot(rec[\"a\"]) - probs"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if (adv > 0 and ratio >= 1 + EPS) or (adv < 0 and ratio <= 1 - EPS):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                pg_grad = 0.0  # clipped"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            else:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                pg_grad = ratio * adv"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            for i in range(N_ACTIONS):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                for j in range(N_FEAT):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                    theta[i][j] += LR * pg_grad * grad_logpi[i] * x[j]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The \"clipped \u2192 zero gradient\" pattern is the heart of PPO. If the new policy has already drifted too far in the beneficial direction, the update stops."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: value and entropy"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Add standard MSE to the critic target and an entropy bonus on the actor, same as A2C."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: diagnostics"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Three things to watch every update:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- **Mean KL** `E[log \u03c0_old - log \u03c0_\u03b8]`. Should stay in `[0, 0.02]`. If it blows past `0.1`, reduce `K_EPOCHS` or `LR`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- **Clip fraction** \u2014 the fraction of samples whose ratio lies outside `[1-\u03b5, 1+\u03b5]`. Should be `~0.1-0.3`. If `~0`, the clip never triggers \u2192 raise `LR` or `K_EPOCHS`. If `~0.5+`, you are over-fitting the rollout \u2192 lower them."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- **Explained variance** `1 - Var(V_target - V_pred) / Var(V_target)`. Critic quality metric. Should climb toward 1 as the critic learns."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **Easy.** Run PPO on 4\u00d74 GridWorld with `\u03b5=0.2, K=4`. Compare sample efficiency to A2C (one epoch per rollout) at matched env steps.\n2. **Medium.** Sweep `K \u2208 {1, 4, 10, 30}`. Plot return vs env steps and track mean KL per update. At what `K` does KL explode on this task?\n3. **Hard.** Replace the clipped surrogate with an adaptive KL penalty (`\u03b2` doubled if `KL > 2\u00b7target`, halved if `KL < target/2`). Compare final return, stability, and clip-free-ness."
      ]
    }
  ],
